WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.980
A deployment plan is a saved list of steps that decides what a package holds.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:10.060
In this video, you create a plan, add and order its steps, and

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:12.520
execute it to download the package.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:20.639
A deployment plan is a named, ordered list of steps.

00:00:20.639 --> 00:00:24.885
Most steps add one kind of data to the package, such as content,

00:00:24.885 --> 00:00:27.130
content definitions, or a file.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:31.088
The steps you can add come from the enabled features.

00:00:31.088 --> 00:00:35.765
When you execute a plan, its steps run from top to bottom and build one package.

00:00:35.765 --> 00:00:40.550
If a step's feature is disabled, the plan keeps the step and marks it unavailable.

00:00:44.765 --> 00:00:47.218
Let's open Tools, Deployments, Plans.

00:00:47.218 --> 00:00:51.439
The page lists the plans of this site, and Add Deployment Plan opens

00:00:51.439 --> 00:00:53.265
the form that creates one.

00:00:54.264 --> 00:00:57.852
A plan needs only a name, and the name must be unique.

00:00:57.852 --> 00:01:00.604
We type Spring Launch and select Create.

00:01:01.074 --> 00:01:03.077
Orchard Core opens the plan.

00:01:03.077 --> 00:01:06.965
Execute and Add Step are at the top, and a message says that

00:01:06.965 --> 00:01:08.614
the plan has no steps.

00:01:12.861 --> 00:01:14.474
Let's select Add Step.

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:19.947
Available Steps lists every step you can add, and Filter narrows the cards by their text.

00:01:19.947 --> 00:01:23.231
The categories on the left group the steps by area.

00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:25.400
Let's open Security.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:30.136
It holds steps such as All Roles and All Users, which export every

00:01:30.136 --> 00:01:33.360
role or every user, with nothing to choose.

00:01:33.819 --> 00:01:38.499
Back under All, we type content in Filter and add Content, which exports

00:01:38.499 --> 00:01:41.379
the items of the content types you choose.

00:01:41.851 --> 00:01:43.293
We check Blog Post.

00:01:43.293 --> 00:01:47.387
The step exports only the published items of the types you check.

00:01:47.387 --> 00:01:52.634
Export As Setup recipe stays unchecked, because it loses references to content items,

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:54.191
and we select Create.

00:01:54.644 --> 00:01:56.959
Let's add Update Content Definitions.

00:01:56.959 --> 00:02:00.997
It exports the definition of a content type, so the site that imports

00:02:00.997 --> 00:02:03.904
the package receives the Blog Post type as well.

00:02:04.393 --> 00:02:10.661
The first checkbox, Include all content types and parts definitions, exports every definition.

00:02:10.661 --> 00:02:13.669
We check Blog Post only and select Create.

00:02:13.669 --> 00:02:17.493
The plan lists each step with a summary of its choices.

00:02:21.784 --> 00:02:27.915
A note under Update Content Definitions says that definitions belong before any content step.

00:02:27.915 --> 00:02:31.384
Let's drag its handle, at the left, above Content.

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:34.624
The order is saved when you drop the step.

00:02:34.624 --> 00:02:39.941
When the plan is executed, the steps run in this order, so the definitions come first.

00:02:40.397 --> 00:02:43.660
Edit reopens a step with its current choices.

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:48.267
Let's select Edit on Content, check Page as well, and select Save.

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:51.147
The step keeps Blog Post and adds Page.

00:02:51.615 --> 00:02:55.531
Delete, on a row or in the editor, removes a step from the

00:02:55.531 --> 00:02:57.305
plan after you confirm.

00:03:01.528 --> 00:03:04.771
Let's select Add Step and the Deployment category.

00:03:04.771 --> 00:03:07.956
It holds the four steps of the Deployment module:

00:03:07.956 --> 00:03:11.778
Custom File, Deployment Plans, JSON Recipe, and Recipe File.

00:03:12.242 --> 00:03:15.328
Custom File adds a file to the package.

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:21.569
Deployment Plans exports the definitions of plans, so another site can recreate them.

00:03:21.569 --> 00:03:25.752
JSON Recipe adds a recipe step that you write yourself.

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:27.724
We add Custom File.

00:03:27.724 --> 00:03:32.582
File Name is the path of the file in the package, and it must be relative.

00:03:32.582 --> 00:03:37.076
File Content is its text, so we type a short note and select Create.

00:03:37.528 --> 00:03:43.851
Recipe File sets the name, description, author, and other details of the recipe in the package.

00:03:43.851 --> 00:03:48.170
File Download reads the first Recipe File step of a plan, so we

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:50.298
add one and name the recipe.

00:03:54.532 --> 00:03:55.960
Let's select Execute.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:58.868
Available Targets lists where the package can go.

00:03:58.868 --> 00:04:03.573
File Download downloads it to your computer, and features such as Remote Deployment

00:04:03.573 --> 00:04:05.212
add targets of their own.

00:04:05.663 --> 00:04:08.914
The Select button on File Download runs the plan.

00:04:08.914 --> 00:04:13.583
Orchard Core runs its steps from top to bottom, and the browser downloads

00:04:13.583 --> 00:04:15.829
a zip file named after the plan.

00:04:15.829 --> 00:04:20.203
If the export fails, an error message appears and nothing downloads.

00:04:20.654 --> 00:04:24.300
Cancel closes Available Targets and leaves the plan as it was.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:28.590
Execute it again whenever you need a package, and the Content step exports

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:31.164
the items that are published at that time.

00:04:32.764 --> 00:04:36.596
The zip holds a recipe, which a site runs when it imports the

00:04:36.596 --> 00:04:39.742
package, and the files of your Custom File steps.

00:04:39.742 --> 00:04:44.204
Steps such as Content add their data to the recipe, in the plan's order.

00:04:44.204 --> 00:04:47.064
A separate video covers importing a package.

00:04:51.288 --> 00:04:54.936
Back on Plans, the search box filters plans by name.

00:04:54.936 --> 00:04:57.074
Each plan has three buttons:

00:04:57.074 --> 00:05:01.728
Manage Steps opens the plan, Edit renames it, and Delete removes it.

00:05:02.199 --> 00:05:04.243
Let's select Edit on this plan.

00:05:04.243 --> 00:05:08.939
We type another name and select Save, and the list returns with a confirmation.

00:05:10.539 --> 00:05:12.755
Two permissions control plans.

00:05:12.755 --> 00:05:18.050
Manage deployment plans lets you create, edit, and delete plans and their steps,

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:20.882
and Export Data lets you execute a plan.

00:05:20.882 --> 00:05:24.699
Administrators have both, and the Plans page needs both.

00:05:26.699 --> 00:05:31.008
A deployment plan lets you choose what a package holds, and in what order.

00:05:31.008 --> 00:05:32.409
Thanks for watching.

